.TH TASKHEALTH-DEMO 1 "August 2026" "TaskHealth 0.2.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
taskhealth-demo \- TaskHealth demonstration program
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B taskhealth-demo
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B taskhealth-demo
connects to a running
.BR taskhealthd (8)
on its default socket and runs five scenarios that exercise the client
library and trigger the daemon's detection engine.  It is a demonstration of
how to use the TaskHealth client API, not an automated test.
.PP
Start
.B taskhealthd
first, then run
.BR taskhealth-demo ,
and watch the daemon's output for alerts.
.SH SCENARIOS
.TP
.B Auto name
Registers a thread with a NULL name and verifies an auto-generated name is
accepted.
.TP
.B Unexpected exit
A registered thread exits without unregistering; the daemon should emit an
UNEXPECTED_EXIT alert.
.TP
.B Deadlock
Two threads lock two mutexes in opposite order; the daemon should emit
DEADLOCK alerts.
.TP
.B Normal heartbeat
A thread heartbeats on schedule; no alert is expected.
.TP
.B Lock wait timeout
A thread blocks on a held mutex longer than its lock-hold threshold; the
daemon should emit a LOCK_WAIT alert.
.PP
A successful run produces 1 UNEXPECTED_EXIT, 3 DEADLOCK, and 1 LOCK_WAIT
alert.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR taskhealthd (8),
.BR taskhealth (7)
